MotionBricks G1 adapter notices

The code under motionbricks/ is vendored unmodified from NVlabs/GR00T-WholeBodyControl
(subproject motionbricks/) at commit 45c03facbf848e0c743091b7d9c17952096ff908 and is
licensed under Apache-2.0 (Part 1 of the LICENSE file in this directory, the
repository's dual-licence notice). The configuration, skeleton and statistics files
under motionbricks/out/ are NVIDIA's plain git files at the same commit.

The checkpoints (G1-clip.ckpt and the pose, root and VQ-VAE models) are NVIDIA's
Git LFS objects at the same commit and are licensed under the NVIDIA Open Model
License (Part 2 of the LICENSE file). The recipe's Model document addresses them by
their LFS oid and size; the platform verifies the bytes when it ingests them.

run.py is a Vonk Forge adapter. It replays the headless navigation loop of upstream
motionbricks/scripts/interactive_demo_g1.py without a viewer or keyboard and writes
the generated G1 qpos trajectory as JSON. MotionBricks has no text encoder; the
command controls style, duration, heading and speed only.

